{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "post_message",
        "description": "Post a message to a board you can read.",
        "parameters": {
            "text": "Round 2, block 3 of 4 (peak): base price 90 credits per MWh. We need to strategize our peak demand charge. Let's plan our actions accordingly.",
            "channel": "public"
        }
    }
}
```

POST_MESSAGE({
  "text": "Team, we're all set for block 4. We charged to full today and will hold for the evening. Let's see how the market plays out for our next moves.",
  "channel": "private"
})

POST_MESSAGE({
  "text": "owner_1: We're charging our battery to full capacity for the morning block, as per our plan. I'll also hold this block.",
  "channel": "private"
})

It seems there might have been a misunderstanding. As Owner_4, I intended to make an announcement about my action before executing it. Let me correct that with the appropriate announcement first:

```json
{
  "name": "announce_action",
  "arguments": {
    "action": "charge",
    "amount": 10,
    "note": "charging for the evening block to store energy at a low base price"
  }
}
```

After announcing my action, I will proceed to charge 10 MWh into my battery for the evening block.

